    <string name="privacy_policy_full">Privacy Policy for QR Scanners\n\nDeveloper: AnakinYoo\n\nCamera and photos\nCamera access is used for real-time scanning. QR Scanners does not intentionally record or upload camera video. Gallery scanning uses Android Photo Picker and processes the selected image for barcode detection without broad photo-library access.\n\nCurrent location\nLocation access is optional. It is requested only when you choose the Location QR type and tap the current-location action. Current coordinates are used to fill latitude and longitude. No background-location permission is requested and coordinates are not uploaded to a developer backend.\n\nLocal history and settings\nScan history, generated content, favorites, and app settings are stored in app-private storage. You can delete individual records or clear all history. Local data remains until you delete it, clear app storage, or uninstall the app, subject to Android platform behavior. App backup is disabled.\n\nSharing and external apps\nWhen you choose to share, open, dial, email, message, add a contact, open a map, or use a Wi-Fi system flow, selected content is handed to the relevant Android system component or external app. Data handled after that handoff is governed by that app or service.\n\nML Kit diagnostics\nBarcode recognition uses Google ML Kit. Google states that ML Kit Android SDKs collect certain device and app information, identifiers, performance metrics, API configuration, feature input and output size, feature version, event types, and error codes for diagnostics and usage analytics. Google states this data is encrypted in transit and the listed ML Kit data is not transferred to third parties. Barcode auto-zoom is not enabled in this app.\n\nDeveloper services\nThe current app has no developer-operated backend, advertising SDK, billing SDK, or custom analytics SDK, and it does not provide user accounts.\n\nPrivacy inquiries\nUse the developer contact mechanism shown on the Google Play listing for QR Scanners. The online Privacy Policy URL published for Google Play must use the same developer identity or app name.</string>
